{"card":{"card_id":"ma-c-27ec9d0f3ae2d5580b87","statement":"The pair $(\\kQ,\\kI)$ is said to be special biserial if\nthe following holds:\n\n- [(G1)] At every vertex of $\\kQ$ at most two arrows end and at most two\narrows start.\n\n- [(G2)] For each arrow $b$ there is at most one arrow $a$ with\n$\\mathfrak{t}(a)=\\mathfrak{s}(b)$ and $ba\\not\\in \\kI$ and at most one arrow $c$ with\n$\\mathfrak{t}(b)=\\mathfrak{s}(c)$ and $cb\\not\\in \\kI$.","source_id":"arXiv:0812.4783","cluster":"representation_theory","statement_sha256":"bafa5460ed6ee783a64e7a0f909b61d7f8fd4e2b71895e687504e77fd9c06f2e","kind":"definition","label":"Definition 4","ref_key":"specialbi","name":"","order":6,"deps":[],"cite_keys":[],"provenance":{"source_url":"https://arxiv.org/abs/0812.4783","harvest_mode":"arxiv_eprint","payload_sha256":"4691b7e6310aff594015f4ee9295f0c5d77eb87af5ba0a297bb3f4cdbb2ee258","line":473,"origin":"latex_env","retrieved_at":"2026-09-29T14:02:07+08:00"},"wash":{"version":"cardwash.v2","stages":["segment","purify","classify","dedupe","emit"],"numbering":"document_order_with_label_heuristic","detail":{"stripped_proof":false,"chars":368,"math_hints":33}}},"paper":{"source_id":"arXiv:0812.4783","title":"Derived tame local and two-point algebras","abstract":"We determine derived representation type of complete finitely generated local and two-point algebras over an algebraically closed field.","authors":["Viktor Bekkert","Yuriy Drozd","Vyacheslav Futorny"],"year":"2008","url":"https://arxiv.org/abs/0812.4783","cluster":"representation_theory","macros":{"lenght":"\\mathop\\mathrm{lenght}\\nolimits","md":"#1\\mbox{-}\\mathrm{mod}","pr":"#1\\mbox{-}\\mathrm{pro}","bp":"\\bullet","iso":"\\simeq","iff":"if and only if","setsuch":"\\left\\{\\,#1\\,|\\,#2\\,\\right\\}","rad":"\\mathop\\mathrm{rad}","End":"\\mathop\\mathrm{End}","im":"\\mathop\\mathrm{Im}","al":"\\alpha","be":"\\beta","la":"\\lambda","Si":"\\Sigma","bA":"\\mathbf A","bB":"\\mathbf B","fR":"\\mathbf r","bL":"\\mathbf L